From: Fedora SL7 Remix contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: reinitialize Romulus MP PHY after resume

Fedora 44's 7.1 kernel moved full-reinitialization policy into the DWC3 glue
properties. Map the existing snps,reinit-phy-on-resume device-tree property to
that policy and enable it on the flattened Romulus multi-port controller.

This is the 7.1 rebase of the three-patch DWC3 series referenced by the SL7
hardware notes.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi | 4 ++++
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c                              | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
@@ -1725,6 +1725,10 @@ &usb_mp {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&usb_mp {
+	snps,reinit-phy-on-resume;
+};
+
 &usb_mp_hsphy0 {
 	vdd-supply = <&vreg_l2e>;
 	vdda12-supply = <&vreg_l2j>;
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -705,6 +705,8 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	probe_data.res = &res;
 	probe_data.ignore_clocks_and_resets = true;
 	probe_data.properties = DWC3_DEFAULT_PROPERTIES;
+	probe_data.properties.needs_full_reinit =
+		device_property_read_bool(dev, "snps,reinit-phy-on-resume");
 	ret = dwc3_core_probe(&probe_data);
 	if (ret)  {
 		ret = dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to register DWC3 Core\n");
-- 
2.51.0

